<div>
  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="African NFT Art Exhibition Featuring Portraits of Two African Royals Launched" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/african-nft-art-exhibition-featuring-potraits-of-two-african-royals-launched.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>The Museum of Modern African Art Gallery & Lifestyle (MOOMA), a platform that promotes African artworks, recently kickstarted a 30-day non-fungible token (NFT) Modern African Art Exhibition. The exhibition, which will be MOOMA’s first NFT showcase, is set to feature the works of Goran Pin or the Portraitist. Pin, a Croatian national, is an artist seen “pushing the edges of the crypto art medium on multiple levels.”</strong>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    According to a statement on MOOMA’s website, taking the centre stage at this exhibition will be the Portratist’s “Kings and Queens Collection.”
  </p><figure id="attachment_460841" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-460841" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-460841 size-full" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists.jpg" alt="" width="1280" height="720" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-768x432.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/nftartists-760x428.jpg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-460841" class="wp-caption-text">The Portraitist – Goran Pin – NFT Artist. The Portraitist is displaying the non-fungible token art collectibles called the “Kings and Queens Collection.”</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    which also contains the “1st ever portraits of African kings minted on the blockchain.” The statement adds:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      It is the first NFT collection of all worlds’ royal families, and 30 of 32 portraits from the Kings and Queens Collection are 1st ever portraits of these persons minted on blockchain at the same time.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    As revealed in the statement, it will be the portraits of two African royals, King Letsie III and King Mswati III that will feature in the Potraitist’s collection.
  </p>
  
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <p>
    In the meantime, the statement also commends Pin for choosing to help connect “traditional art with crypto art.” While his works are “highly collectible”, MOOMA notes that the artist has nonetheless chosen to “put the auction sale of his entire Kings and Queens Collection on hold.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What are your thoughts on this NFT exhibition? You can share your views in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
